{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidGroup","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidGroup","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.PresentedGroup"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.exponentSum_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.exponentSum_σ","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidGroup.lean#L88-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.exponentSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.exponentSum","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidGroup.lean#L82-L86","doc":"**The writhe.** `exponentSum β` is the total exponent sum of any word\nrepresenting `β` — well defined on the group, not merely on words, by\n`lift_const_relators`. This is the `e` of the Morton–Franks–Williams pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.lift_const_relators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.lift_const_relators","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidGroup.lean#L73-L80","doc":"Every Artin relator has total exponent sum zero, so the constant map\n`generator ↦ 1` kills the relators and descends to the quotient. This is the\nwell-definedness obligation for `exponentSum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.σ","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidGroup.lean#L70-L71","doc":"The `i`-th Artin generator `σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.instGroupBraidGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.instGroupBraidGroup","kind":"instance","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidGroup.lean#L67-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.BraidGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.BraidGroup","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidGroup.lean#L64-L65","doc":"The braid group on `n + 1` strands, as the Artin presentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.braidRelators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.braidRelators","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidGroup.lean#L53-L62","doc":"The Artin relators for `n` generators, as elements of the free group.\nFar commutation `σᵢσⱼσᵢ⁻¹σⱼ⁻¹` for `i + 2 ≤ j`, and the braid relation\n`σᵢσᵢ₊₁σᵢ(σᵢ₊₁σᵢσᵢ₊₁)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.strandCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.strandCount","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidGroup.lean#L50-L51","doc":"Number of strands: `BraidGroup n` acts on `n + 1` strands. ","signatureChunk":0}]}